<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Texas Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1835">1835</a>–<a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Texas War of Independence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> Revolution was the rebellion of American settlers and some Tejanos in the Mexican province of Texas against the centralist government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a>. Fighting began in October 1835; Santa Anna won at the Alamo in March 1836, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a> defeated him at San Jacinto on 21 April 1836 and captured him the next day. Texas became an independent republic and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1845.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/texas-revolution.jpg" alt="Texas Revolution" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: original image drawn by Joseph L. Cain; update by karanacs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campaigns_of_the_Texas_Revolution.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The change helped provoke the <b>Texas Revolution</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/first-mexican-republic">First Mexican Republic</a></li></ul></section>
